  "scope": "Exact existing-surface evidence fallback: the preserved source inventory contains 33 official-survey operation entries, exactly matching the immutable count. Shared executable bindings for the same provider method/path are merged into one normalized endpoint. The cited official html_reference artifact is retained as the v2 provenance root; no operation was inferred from a documentation crawl. Prior source-surface scope: Pass B full-surface expansion, re-reviewed against the live v3 API reference (developers.kit.com/api-reference/v3/*, fetched 2026-07-04; the v3 API is deprecated in favor of v4 but Kit's own docs confirm v3 remains live and documented, and this bundle's api_secret-query-param auth is v3-specific and not compatible with v4's API-key-header/OAuth2 scheme, so this expansion stays within v3 rather than rewriting the connector onto an incompatible auth model). 7 read streams (the 5 wave1-pilot streams retained, plus custom_fields/purchases) and 12 write actions covering subscriber/tag/form/sequence/broadcast/custom-field/purchase/webhook lifecycle mutations. Every endpoint below is covered_by a stream/write action XOR excluded with a real category and reason. Exclusions favor breadth of real mutations over: subscription-list sub-resource reads that duplicate the subscribers stream's record shape filtered a different way (duplicate_of); the account endpoint (non_data_endpoint, an account metadata snapshot); and the one genuinely destructive global mutation (unsubscribe, destructive_admin).",
